            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Américo Paredes is a renowned folklorist, academic, educator, novelist, poet, and singer born and raised in Brownsville, Texas in 1915. He was a foundational figure in Mexican American studies and Chicano literature, inspiring several generations of Latino scholars. These interviews were recorded for the Los del Valle Oral History Project, begun in 1993 by Manuel F. Medrano for the purpose of \"collecting and preserving the historical recollections of people in South Texas researched by scholars and underdocumented in archives and published research.\" [Medrano, 2019]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Presented here are the ten unedited and original interviews collected in 1994 and 1995 with Dr. Américo Paredes, and one interview with his older brother Lorenzo Paredes. Across these interviews Américo Paredes chronicles his life "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
